ANNEX
■ Enforcement Decree of the Framework Act on Youth [Annex] <Newly inserted September 12, 2023>

Criteria for revocation of designation of regional centers or the central center (Related to Article 21-6)

1. General criteria
(a) Where there are two or more violations and the applicable disposition criteria differ, the heavier disposition criteria shall apply.
(b) Disposition criteria based on the number of violations shall apply where a disposition has been imposed for the same violation during the past 1 year. When issuing a warning under the individual criteria, if the authority imposing the disposition sets a period of at least 1 month and gives notice to make improvements within that period, but the violation is not remedied, the violation shall be deemed to have been repeated. In such cases, the period shall be calculated by reference to the date on which the disposition was imposed for the violation and the date on which the same violation committed again after that disposition was detected.
(c) Where an aggravated disposition is imposed under item (b), the applicable occurrence level shall be the next level after the level of the disposition imposed before the violation. Where two or more dispositions were imposed within the period under item (b), the highest of their occurrence levels shall serve as that previous level.
(d) Where the authority imposing a disposition considers that a violation under subparagraph 2(b) or (c) resulted from minor carelessness or error, rather than intent or gross negligence, and the applicable disposition criterion is revocation of designation, the authority may reduce the disposition to a warning.

